WEBVTT

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:41.226
The fifth U-17 Japanese team versus

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:44.854
second string shuffle match will now begin.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.524
Representing the U-17 Japanese team are

00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:52.529
No. 6, Ryuji Omagari, and
No. 2, Shuji Tanegashima.

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:56.866
Representing the second string are
Genichiroh Sanada and Jin Akutsu.

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:00.412
Sanada-<i>san </i>and Akutsu-<i>san </i>
are playing doubles?

00:02:01.037 --> 00:02:03.998
This match is gonna be insane.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:13.925
Will you teach me how to
hit that glowing shot?

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:18.430
If you want to do that,
you just need to find

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:20.849
the Super Sweet Spot.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.226
The Super Sweet Potato?

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.270
Not funny.

00:02:26.187 --> 00:02:27.731
Use this.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:34.154
By the time you're able
to play with that racket,

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.488
you'll have figured it out.

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:38.199
Yeah?

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:45.081
"The Emperor and the Monster"

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:53.256
Didn't Akutsu-<i>san </i>quit playing for
a while after the Tokyo prefectural?

00:02:53.757 --> 00:02:56.926
Will he be okay after such a long break?

00:03:07.812 --> 00:03:08.855
Damn it!

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.566
Play tennis in America?

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:14.402
Don't order me around, old man!

00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:18.740
I don't care anymore!

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.287
I gave everything I had against that kid!

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:28.041
That's right. I have no
attachment to tennis anymore!

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:34.297
"I want to play tennis again."

00:03:34.297 --> 00:03:36.299
"I want a real match."

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:39.052
As if I could ever say those things.

00:03:40.512 --> 00:03:41.888
It'd be too uncool!

00:03:42.597 --> 00:03:44.599
It's too late!

00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:53.274
Hey, lucky me. I got a second one.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.610
Today must be my day.

00:03:56.945 --> 00:03:58.697
Hey, Akutsu.

00:03:59.531 --> 00:04:01.908
Want a can of coffee?

00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:08.081
I told you I'd never play tennis again.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:14.337
Okay, if you're able to hit that can into
that garbage can with your racket,

00:04:14.337 --> 00:04:18.299
you'll keep playing. How does that sound?

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:24.139
If you can't, I'll leave without a word.

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:26.641
Idiot.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.687
But if you don't actually try,

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:33.565
you have to rejoin the
Yamabuki tennis team.

00:04:43.491 --> 00:04:45.243
What? Wait...

00:04:53.043 --> 00:04:54.377
Give me that!

00:04:58.214 --> 00:05:01.259
By the way, your lucky color today is black.

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:02.844
Your lucky item is coffee in a ca--

00:05:02.844 --> 00:05:04.095
Shut up!

00:05:17.609 --> 00:05:18.943
Fifteen-love!

00:05:22.447 --> 00:05:25.241
I heard you took a break
from tennis, but this...

00:05:27.494 --> 00:05:29.162
Such incredible power.

00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:31.623
He hasn't lost his touch.

00:05:32.957 --> 00:05:33.958
Akutsu...

00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:36.920
G-Good serve.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:39.923
Give them another one, Jin Akutsu!

00:05:40.507 --> 00:05:43.301
Don't order me around!

00:05:55.063 --> 00:05:57.273
You've got some interesting moves.

00:06:04.781 --> 00:06:07.575
Fierce like the flames!

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:11.538
It's Vice Captain Sanada's
Fu Rin Ka In Zan Rai!

00:06:13.248 --> 00:06:14.249
Really?

00:06:18.586 --> 00:06:21.256
Move like lightning!

00:06:23.425 --> 00:06:25.010
There!

00:06:29.973 --> 00:06:31.099
Game, first string!

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:32.267
One game to love!

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:35.186
The vice captain's technique isn't working?

00:06:35.979 --> 00:06:38.189
It's like scooping goldfish.

00:06:38.606 --> 00:06:41.276
There's no shot I can't return.

00:06:41.735 --> 00:06:42.610
Nyah.

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:48.408
I can't believe he returned Rai so easily.

00:06:49.034 --> 00:06:54.289
And it took everything Tezuka-<i>san</i>
had to deflect it with Phantom...

00:06:56.332 --> 00:06:59.794
Sanada's mind must be agitated.

00:07:03.465 --> 00:07:06.092
Your drink is over there, Senpai!

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:09.054
Oh, sorry.

00:07:13.516 --> 00:07:15.977
Vice Captain, don't let him irritate you.

00:07:15.977 --> 00:07:18.772
He's doing it on purpose.

00:07:18.772 --> 00:07:20.774
I know that!

00:07:20.774 --> 00:07:24.986
You don't have to tell me!
That's not enough to shake my spirit!

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:48.593
How long are you--

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.680
Fifteen-love!

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.435
He's pretty shaken.

00:07:58.353 --> 00:07:59.354
Game, first string!

00:07:59.354 --> 00:08:00.814
Two games to love!

00:08:01.648 --> 00:08:02.691
Game, first string!

00:08:02.691 --> 00:08:04.234
Three games to love!

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:08.780
Sanada, don't get stuck in their rhythm.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:12.659
Nonsense! We'll turn this
match around, Jin Akutsu!

00:08:16.287 --> 00:08:19.791
They're going to give up
on me and go after you.

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.795
So I'll leave the rest to you, Ryuji.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:27.215
Give me a break.

00:08:27.841 --> 00:08:29.384
There we go.

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:34.180
He's making the bearded guy play by himself?

00:08:34.681 --> 00:08:39.894
Is he even allowed to use two rackets at once?

00:08:40.603 --> 00:08:43.648
The rule book doesn't say it's not allowed.

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:46.985
Take this!

00:08:47.652 --> 00:08:50.321
Don't get ahead of yourself!

00:08:52.073 --> 00:08:52.991
Absurd!

00:08:52.991 --> 00:08:56.286
I'll walk all over this farce!

00:08:58.121 --> 00:08:59.247
It's coming! Stand back!

00:08:59.247 --> 00:09:00.707
Don't order me around!

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:04.169
What?

00:09:06.046 --> 00:09:07.213
Fifteen-love!

00:09:08.298 --> 00:09:10.091
Oh, well.

00:09:10.925 --> 00:09:15.013
I'll take you guys on myself.

00:09:21.478 --> 00:09:22.520
Thirty-love!

00:09:24.356 --> 00:09:26.358
We can't attack blindly!

00:09:26.358 --> 00:09:27.567
There's only one of him!

00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:30.528
We'll make him run all over the
court in a battle of attrition!

00:09:30.779 --> 00:09:33.156
I told you not to order me around!

00:09:33.156 --> 00:09:34.491
I'll beat the snot out of you!

00:09:39.204 --> 00:09:43.875
First I'll take away his endurance with Zan...

00:09:44.626 --> 00:09:49.714
I forgot to mention Ryuji has the most
endurance of anyone on the team.

00:09:50.674 --> 00:09:51.591
What?

00:09:53.718 --> 00:09:54.386
In that case...

00:09:58.556 --> 00:09:59.557
Oh, my.

00:09:59.808 --> 00:10:01.434
I-I'm sorry.

00:10:01.893 --> 00:10:02.811
Are you all right?

00:10:08.358 --> 00:10:10.694
Oh, man... This is turning into a brawl!

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:22.914
What?

00:10:22.914 --> 00:10:24.749
Akutsu-<i>san </i>restrained himself?

00:10:25.875 --> 00:10:28.628
He's a sportsman now.

00:10:32.215 --> 00:10:34.426
I'm not going back to Yamabuki.

00:10:34.843 --> 00:10:37.721
To Yamabuki? Then what about to tennis?

00:10:38.388 --> 00:10:39.264
Shut up.

00:10:44.269 --> 00:10:46.980
The moon sure is beautiful tonight.

00:10:49.733 --> 00:10:55.363
Akutsu is feeling the joy
of playing tennis again.

00:10:56.823 --> 00:10:57.657
Wait!

00:10:58.908 --> 00:11:02.579
You may have forgiven me, but I haven't!

00:11:03.246 --> 00:11:04.539
Hit me!

00:11:04.956 --> 00:11:07.959
There it is! The vice captain's "Hit Me!"

00:11:15.216 --> 00:11:17.677
I-I didn't tell you to kick me...

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.222
You're too tense.

00:11:21.222 --> 00:11:23.141
Play your own way.

00:11:32.817 --> 00:11:34.944
You can't hit anything, Shorty.

00:11:36.404 --> 00:11:37.822
Jerk...

00:11:44.913 --> 00:11:47.707
They're starting to work together now.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.628
Sanada's made a complete recovery.

00:11:51.878 --> 00:11:55.548
But they can't beat Ryuji's
double racket style.

00:11:57.384 --> 00:11:59.135
Nothing you do will change the outcome.

00:11:59.552 --> 00:12:00.804
Nonsense!

00:12:02.597 --> 00:12:03.932
If you don't give it up...

00:12:07.435 --> 00:12:08.812
Forty-fifteen!

00:12:10.271 --> 00:12:11.731
What was that?

00:12:11.731 --> 00:12:14.943
It seemed like the ball just moved strangely...

00:12:21.032 --> 00:12:23.201
Your corners are wide open!

00:12:25.912 --> 00:12:26.579
Again...

00:12:28.289 --> 00:12:29.499
Forty-thirty!

00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:31.626
Look at Sanada.

00:12:34.963 --> 00:12:38.049
He swung his racket again
after hitting the ball.

00:12:42.637 --> 00:12:43.888
I see.

00:12:43.888 --> 00:12:47.684
He's forcibly changing the flow
of energy with a second swing.

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:51.688
It happened then, too.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:56.317
A shot seemed to come
from the wrong direction,

00:12:56.317 --> 00:12:57.527
and in the next instant,

00:12:58.153 --> 00:13:00.447
it split my hairband.

00:13:08.371 --> 00:13:09.914
Give me a break.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:14.544
No matter which way it curves,
I'll get the next one.

00:13:15.045 --> 00:13:17.213
Right or left...

00:13:28.058 --> 00:13:29.809
Black Aura...

00:13:30.894 --> 00:13:32.145
I will crush

00:13:32.604 --> 00:13:34.773
your double racket style.

00:13:43.198 --> 00:13:44.657
Damn you...

00:13:46.076 --> 00:13:46.993
Mine.

00:13:49.496 --> 00:13:51.247
Shuji Tanegashima can

00:13:51.247 --> 00:13:54.834
negate and return all special shots.

00:13:57.629 --> 00:14:01.049
He negates all special shots?

00:14:07.263 --> 00:14:11.226
Shu-<i>san </i>has the natural ability
to see the spin of the ball

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:16.147
and instantly convey this
information to his wrists.

00:14:16.564 --> 00:14:18.316
A natural ability?

00:14:18.316 --> 00:14:22.529
I will smash it to smithereens!

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:24.989
Halting Destruction Void.

00:14:28.118 --> 00:14:32.330
He's the only man at this
training camp I couldn't beat.

00:14:33.206 --> 00:14:35.458
Game and first set, first string!

00:14:35.458 --> 00:14:37.085
Six games to love!

00:14:38.461 --> 00:14:40.422
I never lose.

00:14:40.422 --> 00:14:41.172
Nyah.

00:14:42.841 --> 00:14:44.217
First comes rock!

00:14:44.217 --> 00:14:46.302
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:14:46.302 --> 00:14:47.512
Look over there!

00:14:47.929 --> 00:14:49.848
There! There! There!

00:14:50.265 --> 00:14:53.268
V-Vice Captain Sanada sucks at that game...

00:14:54.853 --> 00:14:56.563
We're in the middle of a match!

00:14:56.563 --> 00:14:58.857
If you can't beat me at "look over there,"

00:14:58.857 --> 00:15:00.942
you can't beat us at tennis.

00:15:01.818 --> 00:15:02.777
Move.

00:15:03.486 --> 00:15:04.904
Let me handle this.

00:15:05.822 --> 00:15:07.365
Look over...

00:15:08.616 --> 00:15:11.286
Right... No, left.

00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:15.206
He's keeping up with my movements?

00:15:17.667 --> 00:15:18.668
Then...

00:15:22.005 --> 00:15:22.756
There!

00:15:26.426 --> 00:15:28.303
Akutsu restrained himself!

00:15:28.845 --> 00:15:30.263
A draw...

00:15:30.263 --> 00:15:33.308
Hey, let's play tennis already.

00:15:33.308 --> 00:15:34.225
Fine.

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:37.771
You should be proud.

00:15:38.605 --> 00:15:43.234
You're the only guy I couldn't
beat at "look over there."

00:15:43.234 --> 00:15:44.861
I didn't win.

00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:50.116
But we're not going to lose.

00:15:51.034 --> 00:15:52.827
Second set. Play!

00:15:57.082 --> 00:15:59.417
Try that all you want.
It won't change anything.

00:16:07.092 --> 00:16:09.594
H-He didn't get anywhere near it...

00:16:09.844 --> 00:16:11.388
Of course not.

00:16:11.388 --> 00:16:13.515
I hit the ball somewhere he couldn't get it.

00:16:13.973 --> 00:16:15.850
You weren't even close.

00:16:16.685 --> 00:16:18.144
Shut up, idiot.

00:16:18.144 --> 00:16:20.689
I'll get closer next time.

00:16:28.446 --> 00:16:29.114
There!

00:16:30.073 --> 00:16:33.034
I told you, that won't change anything.

00:16:35.412 --> 00:16:37.747
He used Void again to hit it between them!

00:16:42.919 --> 00:16:45.547
You're in terrible shape, Jin Akutsu.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:48.425
So are you.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:51.970
We have to outsmart him.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:54.556
If once isn't enough, curve it twice.

00:16:54.556 --> 00:16:55.348
What?

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:56.599
He's

00:16:57.058 --> 00:17:00.228
keeping his eyes on every
subtle move you make.

00:17:01.354 --> 00:17:03.523
I'll return his shots.

00:17:03.523 --> 00:17:06.985
You just focus on curving yours.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.166
He swung twice!

00:17:24.169 --> 00:17:25.670
I see.

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:28.506
Try it if you think you can!

00:17:29.257 --> 00:17:31.301
He's curving his trajectories twice.

00:17:31.676 --> 00:17:34.429
Thinking rationally,
just attempting that is reckless.

00:17:36.389 --> 00:17:37.390
Now I know

00:17:38.099 --> 00:17:40.769
why Sanada teamed up with Akutsu.

00:17:42.145 --> 00:17:47.442
Since Sanada has always played
orthodox tennis as an elite,

00:17:47.984 --> 00:17:51.654
he needed Akutsu's unconventional style.

00:17:52.572 --> 00:17:55.033
He understood that better than anyone.

00:17:55.492 --> 00:17:58.995
That's why he's playing doubles with Akutsu?

00:17:59.454 --> 00:18:01.331
When you played each other,

00:18:01.748 --> 00:18:04.459
Genichiroh's spirit was crushed.

00:18:05.669 --> 00:18:10.757
That must have drawn out
his latent fighting spirit.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.135
The same goes for Akutsu.

00:18:15.387 --> 00:18:18.890
What he needed most right now was

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:22.644
a head-to-head fighter like Sanada-<i>kun</i>.

00:18:23.144 --> 00:18:25.647
That's why he accepted his invitation.

00:18:26.356 --> 00:18:29.818
I don't care if it makes me uncool!

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:33.738
I'll give this match everything I have!

00:18:36.658 --> 00:18:38.660
98 more centimeters!

00:18:41.663 --> 00:18:43.206
75!

00:18:46.459 --> 00:18:48.253
44!

00:18:49.671 --> 00:18:51.172
Take this!

00:19:00.974 --> 00:19:03.601
Th-That was incredible, Vice Captain!

00:19:04.269 --> 00:19:08.523
Even Shu-<i>san </i>couldn't handle two curves.

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:12.110
Double Clutch...

00:19:29.753 --> 00:19:33.048
It's no use. It only curved once.

00:19:33.048 --> 00:19:36.801
It's not good enough until he fully masters it.

00:19:45.018 --> 00:19:46.811
H-He reached it!

00:19:47.437 --> 00:19:49.731
Don't give up, Sanada!

00:19:50.857 --> 00:19:52.359
You can do it!

00:19:52.817 --> 00:19:54.736
Right, partner?

00:19:56.196 --> 00:19:56.863
Yeah!

00:20:03.536 --> 00:20:05.163
Curve once more!

00:20:05.538 --> 00:20:07.082
Curve!

00:20:08.041 --> 00:20:10.502
Curve twice!

00:20:13.296 --> 00:20:14.089
It's coming!

00:20:20.679 --> 00:20:22.514
Game and match, first string!

00:20:22.514 --> 00:20:24.557
Tanegashima-Omagari pair!

00:20:27.686 --> 00:20:28.812
A match

00:20:29.354 --> 00:20:30.814
is a merciless thing.

00:20:32.691 --> 00:20:33.483
But...

00:20:34.192 --> 00:20:38.029
I think a new fire burns within Sanada.

00:20:39.364 --> 00:20:43.034
Perfect your Double Clutch
before you challenge us again.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:49.040
I'll master the Triple Clutch and
then come back to challenge you.

00:20:51.084 --> 00:20:52.419
Hey, you.

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:57.799
Never mind.

00:21:00.677 --> 00:21:04.139
Looks like Akutsu has a new reason

00:21:04.639 --> 00:21:06.516
to keep playing tennis.

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:15.066
You've finally got the hang of it, Shorty.

00:21:16.109 --> 00:21:18.278
That concludes my lesson.

00:21:18.278 --> 00:21:19.946
Go on.

00:21:20.447 --> 00:21:22.907
But I want to play you.

00:21:24.993 --> 00:21:26.828
Hey, Brother!

00:21:27.954 --> 00:21:30.290
Let's have a real match!

00:21:33.001 --> 00:21:35.754
You want a real match?

00:21:36.004 --> 00:21:36.671
Huh?

00:21:37.839 --> 00:21:40.175
A real match?

00:21:41.885 --> 00:21:44.554
That's right. A real match.

00:23:18.398 --> 00:23:19.482
"Next Time"

00:23:19.482 --> 00:23:21.443
"Next Time"
The time has finally come, Oni.

00:23:21.443 --> 00:23:22.152
The time has finally come, Oni.

00:23:22.152 --> 00:23:26.740
Yeah. I've waited so long for
Tokugawa to beat Byodoin and stand

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:28.324
at the top of the Japanese team!

00:23:28.575 --> 00:23:30.368
Are you crying?

00:23:30.368 --> 00:23:31.745
N-No!

00:23:33.288 --> 00:23:36.291
Despite your looks, you're quite a crybaby.

00:23:37.208 --> 00:23:38.460
Don't worry.

00:23:38.460 --> 00:23:40.337
I know he'll do it.

00:23:40.837 --> 00:23:44.257
"Resolve"
The next episode of
<i>New Prince of Tennis </i>is: "Resolve."

00:23:44.257 --> 00:23:48.480
"Resolve"
Tokugawa, go fulfill your promise!
